config MI_LAUNCH_BOOST
	tristate "Xiaomi app launch boost (iorap2)"
	depends on MMU
	depends on MULTIUSER
	select TRACEPOINTS
	help
	  Kernel module for accelerating Android application cold start by
	  collecting file page access patterns during app launch and
	  performing predictive page pre-reading on subsequent launches.

	  The module hooks into the VFS read and page fault paths to record
	  which file pages an application accesses during startup. On later
	  launches of the same app, it pre-reads those pages into the page
	  cache, reducing I/O wait time during cold start.

	  Features:
	    - File page access pattern collection via vendor hooks
	    - Bitmap-based page tracking per file (up to 2GB per file)
	    - Multi-app tracking with LRU eviction (up to 100 apps)
	    - PTE-level hot page snapshot and swap-in acceleration
	    - Debug interface via /proc/iorap_node/

	  If unsure, say N.

config MI_LAUNCH_BOOST_PTE_PREREAD
	bool "PTE-based hot page snapshot and pre-reading"
	depends on MI_LAUNCH_BOOST
	default y
	help
	  Enable Page Table Entry (PTE) level hot page detection. This
	  feature walks the process page tables to identify pages that are
	  both referenced and young (actively used), then pre-reads them
	  via swap-in (anonymous pages) or fadvise (file pages).

	  This provides more accurate pre-reading than file-level
	  collection alone, as it captures the actual working set of
	  the application at the PTE level.

	  If unsure, say Y.

config MI_LAUNCH_BOOST_FILE_PREREAD
	bool "File-based pre-reading via vfs_fadvise"
	depends on MI_LAUNCH_BOOST
	depends on MI_LAUNCH_BOOST_PTE_PREREAD
	default n
	help
	  Enable file-based pre-reading using vfs_fadvise(WILLNEED).
	  This feature is used alongside PTE preread to pre-load file
	  pages identified during the snapshot phase.

	  Note: This is currently disabled by default as the PTE-based
	  approach handles file pages through the generic prepage path.

	  If unsure, say N.
